<resources>
    <!-- Splash Screen Icon Guidelines -->
    <!-- 
    ANDROID SPLASH SCREEN ICON REQUIREMENTS:
    
    The splash screen icon appears in a circular container at the center of the screen.
    Common issues and solutions:
    
    1. VERTICAL SQUASHING: This happens when the icon is too tall or doesn't fit the circular container properly.
    
    2. RECOMMENDED ICON SPECS:
       - Format: PNG with transparency
       - Size: 288×288 dp (this is the standard Android splash screen icon size)
       - Aspect Ratio: 1:1 (square) or designed to fit in a circle
       - Safe Zone: Keep important elements within 192×192 dp center area
       - Background: Transparent
       - Padding: Include at least 48dp padding around your logo
    
    3. DESIGN TIPS:
       - Create a square canvas (288×288 dp) in Photoshop
       - Place your logo in the center with proper padding
       - Ensure the logo fits well within a circular mask
       - Test with circular cropping to see how it will appear
    
    4. ALTERNATIVE SOLUTIONS:
       - Use a circular background behind your logo
       - Create a version of your logo specifically for splash screens
       - Consider using just the icon part of your logo (without text)
    
    5. TESTING:
       - Build and install the app
       - Cold start the app to see the splash screen
       - The icon should appear centered and properly proportioned
    -->
</resources>
